<title>USA: OG&amp;E Electric to lower rates by $50 million.</title>
<headline>OG&amp;E Electric to lower rates by $50 million.</headline>
<dateline>OAKLAHOMA CITY, Okla. 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>OG&amp;E Electric Services said it received approval from the Oklahoma Corporate Commission to lower its rates by $50 million.</p>
<p>The company said $45 million would be implemented in 1997 and the remaining $5 million in 1998.</p>
<p>The move means the average OG&amp;E residential customer will see an 8.1 percent -- or about $7.65 reduction -- in their bills during the months of June through October, the company said.</p>
</text>
